# Pre-Commit Checks

Before creating any `git commit`, always run the following checks and fix any failures.

## Required Checks

1. **Bats tests**: Run `bats tests/` when `vstorm` / templates / helpers / workload / bats tests change
2. **Python unit tests**: Run `python3 -m unittest discover -s monitoring/tests -v` when `monitoring/workload-result/`, `monitoring/tests/`, or `monitoring/scripts/` change
3. **Dashboard JS unit tests**: Run `node --test monitoring/tests/test_dashboard_lib.js` when `monitoring/workload-result/static/` or that test file changes
4. **YAML lint**: Run `yamllint` on any changed plain YAML files (`helpers/`, `workload/`, `monitoring/yaml/`, `monitoring/tests/fixtures/`, `.github/workflows/`; not `templates/`)
5. **Markdown lint**: Run `markdownlint-cli2` on any changed `.md` files

## Rules

- If any check fails, **fix the issue before committing** -- do not commit broken code
- Never use `--no-verify` to bypass pre-commit hooks
- After committing, run `git status` to verify the commit succeeded
- If a pre-commit hook rejects the commit, fix the reported issue and create a new commit (do not amend)

## Check Commands

```bash
# Bats
bats tests/

# Monitoring / workload-result Python tests
python3 -m unittest discover -s monitoring/tests -v

# Dashboard JS helpers (node built-in test runner)
node --test monitoring/tests/test_dashboard_lib.js

# Lint YAML (same globs as CI)
yamllint helpers/*.yaml workload/*.yaml monitoring/yaml/*.yaml \
  monitoring/tests/fixtures/*.yaml .github/workflows/*.yaml

# Lint Markdown (check changed files)
markdownlint-cli2 "**/*.md"
```
